\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Model comparison across different architectures and training strategies. ResNet18 fine-tuned achieved the best validation accuracy (89.78\%) with efficient training dynamics. Transfer learning (frozen backbone) performed poorly across all architectures. Note: validation set at this stage included both clean and occluded images; the small portion of occluded images does not invalidate model selection decisions.}}{10}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:model_comparison}{{8}{10}{Model comparison across different architectures and training strategies. ResNet18 fine-tuned achieved the best validation accuracy (89.78\%) with efficient training dynamics. Transfer learning (frozen backbone) performed poorly across all architectures. Note: validation set at this stage included both clean and occluded images; the small portion of occluded images does not invalidate model selection decisions}{figure.8}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Mean batch composition before weighted sampling: batches are heavily dominated by empty squares and pawns, with rare pieces (queens, bishops, rooks) barely represented. This imbalance causes poor minority class learning.}}{10}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:batch_imbalance}{{9}{10}{Mean batch composition before weighted sampling: batches are heavily dominated by empty squares and pawns, with rare pieces (queens, bishops, rooks) barely represented. This imbalance causes poor minority class learning}{figure.9}{}}
